<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kurda</h1><p class="st-meta">1780 BCE – 1761 BCE (approx.) · capital Kurda</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small kingdom of the Sinjar region known from the Mari letters, one of the rival states that filled the gap left by Shamshi-Adad's empire.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kurda lay in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinjar-mountains">Sinjar</a> plain of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, probably near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-andarig">Andarig</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-karana">Karana</a>; its site is not identified. It emerged as an independent kingdom when the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-upper-mesopotamia">Kingdom of Upper Mesopotamia</a> dissolved around 1776 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mari">Mari</a> letters name a king Simah-ilane and later a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi-of-kurda">Hammurabi of Kurda</a>, not to be confused with his famous namesake of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>. Kurda's rulers concluded and broke oaths with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mari">Mari</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-andarig">Andarig</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eshnunna">Eshnunna</a> and Babylon, and their envoys appear at the courts of greater kings. Nothing is known of its institutions beyond this diplomatic record.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hammurabi">Hammurabi</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> conquered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mari">Mari</a> in 1761 BCE, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinjar-mountains">Sinjar</a> kingdoms fell under Babylonian control, and Kurda drops out of the record.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1780 BCE – 1761 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:24.28%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1780 BCE – 1761 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kurda</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Simah-ilane, Hammurabi of Kurda</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Mesopotamian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Akkadian, Amorite</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Iraq</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kurda</dd></dl></aside></div>

